  "title": "The associative-commutative spectrum of SC229",
  "batch_label": "新WIN-1批次",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For A={0,1,2} with operation table rows (0,0,0), (1,0,1), (1,1,1), and every finite nonempty fixed label set I, two full linear binary terms on I (each variable once, arbitrary order, no constants) induce the same function A^I -> A if and only if their leftmost-decomposition trees agree as rooted labelled trees with exactly one distinguished child at each nonleaf and all other children unordered. Every such decorated tree is realised. Hence for every n>=1 the number c_n of these term functions is (n-1)! times the sum, for k=0,...,n-1, of binom(n,k) k^(n-1-k)/(n-1-k)!, with 0^0=1. Equivalently T(x)=sum_{n>=1}c_n x^n/n! satisfies T=x(1+T exp(T)); a direct integer recurrence and a function-only recursive decoder are supplied. This resolves the exact all-n counting question in source.md at its frozen interpretation in problem.md.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
